 in consonance with a council of male and female chiefs.”  “According to tradition, the first Alafin and founder of Oyo was Oranyan or Oranmiyan, youngest son (or, in some accounts, grandson) of Oduduwa, the legendary hero and father of all the Yoruba. The Alafin’s title describes him  as Lord of the Palace (Afin), but his authority is that of King (Oba) of the Oyo, and he is also ‘Lord of the World and of Life’, ‘Owner of the Land’; and ‘Companion of the gods.’” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 948, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 864})
