r conquests. As victorious Carolingian armies withdrew they were often – as we have seen – replaced by missionaries, charged with winning the hearts and souls of the conquered, and with establishing their obedience to the Frankish Church (and, therefore, empire).” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 845, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 756})
