ally succeeded for the first time in becoming members of the elite’.”“[…] from the time of Euergetes II. No longer was it essential to be Greek to succeed in post-Ptolemy VIII Euergetes II Egypt. The elite ruled, whether Greek or Egyptian.’ “[…] the exclusive Greco-Macedonian hold on power in Egypt was ended, substituted by […] a vastly inferior intelligentsia made up of the Alexandrian citizen-body of mixed race.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 922, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 790})
